Required Review Output Format

When asked to review a UiPath project, always return the following structure.

Executive Summary
Overall risk: Low / Medium / High
Production readiness: Ready / Needs fixes / Not ready
Main concern:
Review confidence: High / Medium / Low
Findings

For each finding use this format:

[Severity] Finding title
Finding ID:
Rule:
File / Workflow:
Evidence:
Why it matters:
Suggested fix:
Fix eligibility: Auto-fixable / Semi-auto-fixable / Manual-only
Fix risk: Low / Medium / High
Confidence: High / Medium / Low

Severity must be one of:

Critical
Warning
Suggestion
Manual Check
Manual Checks

List items that cannot be fully verified from repository files alone.

Examples:

Whether selectors actually work against the live application
Whether Orchestrator assets exist in the target environment
Whether mail filters match business expectations
Whether queue references are unique in production data
Whether CI/CD pipeline resolves internal dependencies
Whether Workflow Analyzer reports errors
Whether PDD confirms exception classification
Recommended Next Actions

Return 3 to 7 prioritized next actions.

Important

Do not provide generic UiPath best practices unless they are tied to an observed issue.

Do not modify files unless explicitly asked.

If a review artifact is requested or this is a full project review, write the result to .review/rpa-review-result.md.
